# Content coverage vs slide budget

**Status:** shipped 2026-09-06. Do not restore `Total Target Slide Count: ~N` or a global 14/17/35 generation cap.

## Product stance (live)

- **Content drives length.** Duration still matters (~15–20 min best practice, not over ~30 min); beyond ~30–40 min, split into two/three courses rather than dropping objectives. Duration warning/split is **not** in this cut.
- **One module per terminal** (hard).
- **1–2 teaching slides per enabling** (hard). One slide minimum; second slide only to chunk. Do not put two enablings on one slide. If a listed enabling is not taught, QC `coverage` error.
- Chrome (titles, overviews, summaries, KCs, exam) still comes from Course Settings toggles.
- Leftover `slideCount` in saved Course Settings is storage-only and is **not** passed into the outline prompt.

## Implementation

- Outline + post-process: [`src/lib/enablingCoverage.ts`](src/lib/enablingCoverage.ts), [`src/services/aiService.ts`](src/services/aiService.ts) `generateCourseOutline`.
- Hydrate keeps `enablingIndex`.
- QC: [`src/services/structuralValidator.ts`](src/services/structuralValidator.ts) `coverage` issues.
- Course structure shows “Enabling N” on teaching slides.

## Not in this cut

- Fuller source extract (12k / 4k windows).
- Narration word-count duration meter + split prompt.
